        "original_id": "55fb0d5f-0579-5967-a0df-4623771b0193",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: KSPN-FM\n- People: Tom Petty, Van Morrison, Ben Harper, Stephen Thomas Erlewine\n- Bands: Talking Heads, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, Widespread Panic\n- Music formats and genres: AAA format, classic rock, new wave, punk, art rock, funk, world music\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Talking Heads were an American rock band formed in 1975 in New York City.\n- Talking Heads remained active until 1991.\n- Critic Stephen Thomas Erlewine described Talking Heads as one of the most critically acclaimed bands of the 1980s.\n- Talking Heads helped pioneer new wave music by integrating punk, art rock, funk, and world music with avant-garde sensibilities and an anxious, clean-cut image.\n- KSPN-FM features the AAA format.\n- KSPN-FM's AAA format combines classic rock hits from Tom Petty, Van Morrison, and Talking Heads with newer musicians such as Ben Harper, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, and Widespread Panic.",
